s with a joint-history note explaining that it comes from the sibling question's experiment and is cited only for the term shape this account did not cover, and appended one sentence to the rationale. Nothing else changed: the account keeps its own experiment, its own receipt and its violated conclusion, and the remaining limits are the ones that still hold.\\\",\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n   \\\"investigation_id\\\": i['investigation_id'],\n   \\\"experiment_id\\\": i['experiment_id'],\n   \\\"joint_history\\\": \\\"The second receipt cited here was produced by a separate producer experiment, 5cee23d4545c4f4fb34e741a7d2cb374-experiment, filed under the sibling question @timeoutnow_campaign_chain rather than by this account's own experiment. It is compatible because it runs the same fixture family - three real voters from equal snapshots at index=10/term=1 with CheckQuorum and PreVote, one real election, one heartbeat, hand-delivered messages through the documented inbound path - and because the shape it supplies is the one this account's own receipt lacks: a message whose term exceeds the receiver's own.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\": i['source_ids'],\n   \\\"executions\\\": {\\\"5d829fd30b3649f8bb9ef79e6bb3d624\\\":[59,60,61,62], \\\"026b6c86522d454299d1f3ca358c009e\\\":[67,69]},\n   \\\"conclusion\\\": i['conclusion'],\n   \\\"defect_claim\\\": i['defect_claim'],\n   \\\"rationale\\\": rat,\n   \\\"knowledge\\\": i.get('knowledge', []),\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\": i['counterevidence'],\n   \\\"limitations\\\": lims\n }]}\njson.dump(u, open('draft/update.json','w'), indent=1)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -m consensus_assurance.cli validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_00-04-05-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
